  "name": "Roofs",
  "_about": "WHAT A ROOF OR A DOME IS COVERED WITH: rows of glazed tube tiles (a Chinese roof), Roman coppi, slates, fish-scale tiles, sheets of lead or copper with their seams, gold leaf; and the patterned coverings -- the Stephansdom's glazed zigzags, St Basil's stripes, spirals and diamonds, glazed diamonds (El Pilar, the Zsolnay roofs of Budapest). On a dome or a round roof u runs round it (a whole number of tiles each way round, so the rows meet) and v up the slope: the rows of a round roof converge toward its crown as they do on the real ones.",
